---
/**
 * HiloTricolor (design-system.md §7.12, item 12; design/ds/canvas/Elementos.dc.html
 * block "HILOTRICOLOR"): a 3px line in three equal solid thirds — yellow /
 * blue / red, the only place in the whole UI where the Venezuelan tricolor
 * appears in full (design-system.md §3.3, "tricolor solo en HiloTricolor...
 * nunca como fondo, botón o acento de UI"). Detail of `Pie` (SM-028) or of a
 * future edition badge, never a generic section divider.
 *
 * The three colors are fixed and carry no props (backlog SM-024, "sin props
 * de color"; PLAN.md §5, "el tricolor es fijo"): the `.hilo-tricolor` class
 * in theme.css supplies the 3px height and the hard-stopped gradient that
 * renders as three solid blocks. `ancho` (PLAN.md §5) is the only prop, for
 * a narrower badge use case; it is applied as an inline style because
 * Tailwind's `w-*` utilities need a literal class string at build time and
 * cannot take an arbitrary value from a runtime prop.
 *
 * Purely decorative — it carries no information of its own — so it is
 * `aria-hidden`.
 *
 * The scroll-triggered sweep of design-system.md §11.4 (`data-entrada="hilo"`)
 * is SM-069 (Fase 2, movimiento) and out of this ticket's scope: this
 * component renders only the static line. `theme.css` already scopes that
 * animation to elements carrying `[data-entrada='hilo']`, so omitting the
 * attribute here is enough to leave it unanimated for now.
 *
 * No position classes are accepted here (diseno-web-indice.md, decision 13):
 * a caller that needs to place this within a layout wraps it instead.
 */
interface Props {
  /** CSS width value. Defaults to 100%, the `Pie` use case. */
  ancho?: string;
}

const { ancho = '100%' } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="hilo-tricolor" aria-hidden="true" style={`width: ${ancho};`}></div>
